This repository contains a format specification, two reference implementations, a
conformance suite, the research papers behind the format, and the generator for
anla.evemisslab.com.

ANLA-MVP v0.1 is a research profile. It is tested, but it is young: an archive in
this format should not be the only copy of anything that cannot be lost. See
SECURITY.md for what the format does and does not protect against, and SPEC.md
section 13 for what it does not implement.

The format builds on published standards and takes ideas from published work,
none of which is affiliated with or endorses this project: SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4),
DEFLATE and zlib (RFC 1951, RFC 1950), CRC-32 (ISO/IEC 13239), JSON (RFC 8259),
ZIP (PKWARE APPNOTE), and — as prior art discussed in the papers — IPLD CAR, the
OCI Image Specification, BagIt (RFC 8493), Zstandard (RFC 8878), BLAKE3 and
FastCDC.

